+    "## 2. Original evidential classifier\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The evidential model uses the same current `CategoricalDNN` class imported by the original notebook, retaining its loss, annealing schedule, and regularization defaults as well as the YAML settings. The original model already specifies the correct input/output widths; these are checked against the dataset schema.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Notation aligned with the paper (Eqs. 3–7).** The index $n$ denotes an input/observation and $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,K\\}$ denotes a class ($K=4$ here). The class indicator $y_{n,k}$ is 1 when the observed class is $k$ and 0 otherwise. The network produces nonnegative evidence $e_{n,k}$, giving\n",
+    "\\[\n",
+    "\\alpha_{n,k}=e_{n,k}+1,\\qquad\n",
+    "S_n=\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\\alpha_{n,k},\\qquad\n",
+    "\\boldsymbol p_n\\sim\\operatorname{Dir}(\\boldsymbol\\alpha_n).\n",
+    "\\]\n",
+    "Here $\\boldsymbol p_n$ is the **latent probability vector**. The predicted probability is its mean (Eq. 4):\n",
+    "\\[\n",
+    "\\widehat p_{n,k}=\\mathbb E[p_{n,k}]\n",
+    "=\\frac{\\alpha_{n,k}}{S_n}.\n",
+    "\\]\n",
+    "We write $S_n$ to make explicit the observation dependence of the paper's $S$. Classification $\\alpha_{n,k}$ is a Dirichlet parameter; it is distinct from the NIG shape parameter $\\alpha_n$ used in the regression notebooks. Belief mass and DST uncertainty mass (Eqs. 5–7), written with an observation index, are\n",
+    "\\[\n",
+    "b_{n,k}=\\frac{e_{n,k}}{S_n},\\qquad\n",
+    "u_n=\\frac{K}{S_n},\\qquad\n",
+    "u_n+\\sum_k b_{n,k}=1.\n",
+    "\\]\n",
+    "\n",
+    "In the code, `probability` contains $\\widehat p_{n,k}$, while `ale`, `epi`, and `u` contain the aleatoric variances, epistemic variances, and $u_n$, respectively. These predicted probabilities are not draws of the latent $p_{n,k}$.\n"
+   ]
