+    "## Interpreting these results\n",
+    "\n",
+    "All reported errors and standard deviations are in friction-velocity units (m/s); variances are in (m/s)². Predictive intervals concern future target values, not confidence intervals for the fitted mean. Coverage, width, and NLL complement prediction error; low error alone does not validate uncertainty. Day-grouped test observations can still be dependent. The original one/five-epoch demonstrations may be undertrained, and this notebook deliberately retains that training budget rather than changing it to improve the displayed results.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The original short evidential fit can produce very large variances when ν is small or α approaches one. Heavy tails can give a large standard deviation even when a central predictive interval is narrower. The uncertainty panel uses a symmetric-log axis when needed to display this range without removing observations.\n"
