+    "## Evidential and dropout uncertainty\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For each class, the paper's law-of-total-variance decomposition (Eqs. 20–23) is\n",
+    "\\[\n",
+    "\\underbrace{\\mathbb E[\\operatorname{Var}(y_{n,k}\\mid p_{n,k})]}_{\\text{aleatoric}}\n",
+    "=\\mathbb E[p_{n,k}(1-p_{n,k})]\n",
+    "=\\widehat p_{n,k}(1-\\widehat p_{n,k})\\frac{S_n}{S_n+1},\n",
+    "\\]\n",
+    "\\[\n",
+    "\\underbrace{\\operatorname{Var}(\\mathbb E[y_{n,k}\\mid p_{n,k}])}_{\\text{epistemic}}\n",
+    "=\\operatorname{Var}(p_{n,k})\n",
+    "=\\frac{\\widehat p_{n,k}(1-\\widehat p_{n,k})}{S_n+1}.\n",
+    "\\]\n",
+    "Their sum is the total class-indicator variance\n",
+    "\\[\n",
+    "\\operatorname{Var}(y_{n,k})\n",
+    "=\\widehat p_{n,k}(1-\\widehat p_{n,k}).\n",
+    "\\]\n",
+    "The variance traces plotted below sum the corresponding per-class variances over $k$ for each observation $n$; they are not variances across observations. The separate statistic `K / sum(alpha)` is the paper's DST uncertainty mass $u_n=K/S_n$ (Eq. 6), also called **evidential vacuity**. It is not an additive variance component.\n",
+    "\n",
