+    "=\\frac{\\alpha_{n,k}}{S_n}.\n",
+    "\\]\n",
+    "We write $S_n$ to make explicit the observation dependence of the paper's $S$. Classification $\\alpha_{n,k}$ is a Dirichlet parameter; it is distinct from the NIG shape parameter $\\alpha_n$ used in the regression notebooks. Belief mass and DST uncertainty mass (Eqs. 5–7), written with an observation index, are\n",
+    "\\[\n",
+    "b_{n,k}=\\frac{e_{n,k}}{S_n},\\qquad\n",
