+    "## Original 10-class model\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The CLS hidden state feeds the original linear head. Dirichlet moments obey `total = aleatoric + epistemic`; the Dempster–Shafer score `K / sum(alpha)` is reported separately and is not a variance. Uncertainty methods return detached NumPy arrays.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Classification notation from the paper.** For classification, $n$ indexes observations and $k$ indexes classes. Code `alpha` denotes the paper's Dirichlet $\\alpha_{n,k}$, not the NIG regression parameter $\\alpha_n$. Write $S_n=\\sum_k\\alpha_{n,k}$ (the paper writes $S$ at a fixed input). Class probabilities are $\\hat p_{n,k}=\\alpha_{n,k}/S_n$ [Eq. (4)]. The classwise `aleatoric` and `epistemic` fields correspond to $\\mathbb{E}[p_{n,k}(1-p_{n,k})]$ [Eqs. (20)–(21)] and $\\operatorname{Var}(p_{n,k})$ [Eqs. (22)–(23)]. Their sum is $\\hat p_{n,k}(1-\\hat p_{n,k})$. The Dempster–Shafer uncertainty mass is $u_n=K/S_n$ for $K$ classes; it is a different quantity. Any reported sum of class variances is a covariance trace, not a regression variance.\n"
    ]
   },
