+    "| `epistemic` | $\\operatorname{Var}(\\mu_n)=\\beta_n/[\\nu_n(\\alpha_n-1)]$ | (26) |\n",
+    "| `total` | $\\mathbb{E}[\\sigma_n^2]+\\operatorname{Var}(\\mu_n)$ | (19), applied to the NIG model |\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Expectations and variances above are evaluated at the **same fixed input** under its predicted NIG distribution; they are not calculated across different test rows. Code arrays apply these formulas separately to every row and target. Predictive NLL, PIT, and intervals use the Student-t distribution in Eq. (15), with location $\\gamma_n$, $2\\alpha_n$ degrees of freedom, and squared scale $\\beta_n(1+\\nu_n)/(\\nu_n\\alpha_n)$. Its scale is not its standard deviation. Raw network parameters use the training target scale; evaluation converts locations and variances to the original target units, with variances multiplied by the squared inverse scaling factor.\n",
