+    "The original `training_var=[0.0033433]` is retained as metadata. A variance alone does not identify the mean offset or a complete target transformation: without a fitted scaler, predictions and variances stay in **model target units**. Passing the scaler fitted during training transforms means once and variances by its squared inverse slope. It must not be fitted on the test set. Thus the notation key applies in whichever target units are actually available; physical units require the saved training scaler when the model was trained on transformed targets.\n"
