+    "## 11. Optional diurnal composite, following Figure 11\n",
+    "For a quantity with a meaningful daily cycle, this plot follows Figure 11 of [Schreck et al. (2024), *Evidential Deep Learning: Enhancing Predictive Uncertainty Estimation for Earth System Science Applications*](https://doi.org/10.1175/AIES-D-23-0093.1), *Artificial Intelligence for the Earth Systems*, 3, e230093: blue triangles for the observed mean, orange squares for the predicted mean, green circles for aleatoric standard deviation, and red pentagons for epistemic standard deviation against **clock time**. It complements the chronological plot above. A diurnal composite is appropriate only when pooling the same time of day across dates answers the scientific question; retain the date plot for nonperiodic data. Disable this optional section when a daily cycle is not meaningful for your dataset. Related stations, subjects, or regimes may need separate composites.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The composite uses **all held-out rows**, with 10-minute clock-time bins. Let $B_t$ contain the observations in bin $t$. Its observed and predicted means are $|B_t|^{-1}\\sum_{n\\in B_t}y_n$ and $|B_t|^{-1}\\sum_{n\\in B_t}\\gamma_n$. Following Eqs. (25) and (26), the separate uncertainty curves are\n",
+    "\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{|B_t|}\\sum_{n\\in B_t}\\mathbb{E}[\\sigma_n^2]}\n",
+    "\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n",
+    "\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{|B_t|}\\sum_{n\\in B_t}\\operatorname{Var}(\\mu_n)}.\n",
+    "$$\n",
+    "\n",
+    "These are root-mean-square conditional standard deviations, computed separately for each target from the physical-unit variances above. They are not means of standard deviations, standard errors of the bin means, or predictive intervals. They also exclude between-observation variation in predicted means; they are **not** the total uncertainty of a time-bin mixture. Bin counts and the aggregated values are saved for inspection.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Dates without timezone information retain their source clock; timestamps with explicit offsets were normalized to UTC by the plotting configuration above. Numeric elapsed time does not identify a time of day and is skipped. The default uses the authors' Cabauw data and unchanged one-pass regression settings; its plotted values are this notebook's results, **not a reproduction of the paper's trained-model results**. For your data, optionally supply target display names and physical units below; do not infer units from model outputs.\n"
