+    "\n",
+    "`ale_sum` and `epi_sum` sum the corresponding variances over classes (covariance traces), not the variance of the sum of one-hot labels. In later cells, variables reassigned with `np.sqrt` contain standard deviations; for example, `total = np.sqrt(ale_sum + epi_sum)` is the square root of the total covariance trace. DST $u_n$ is distinct from epistemic variance. The ensemble sections apply Eq. (19) to the same class events across members. The original external evaluation files are required to run these research figures.\n"
