+   "source": [
+    "## Notation guide: regression equations in the paper\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For sample $n$, the evidential network outputs $(\\gamma_n,\\nu_n,\\alpha_n,\\beta_n)$, Eqs. (12)–(15). The paper's $\\mu_n$ is an uncertain latent mean; its expectation is $\\gamma_n$.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "| Code/data alias in the evidential sections | Paper notation |\n",
+    "|---|---|\n",
+    "| `mu`, prediction columns ending `_pred` | $\\gamma_n=\\mathbb{E}[\\mu_n]$, Eq. (24) |\n",
+    "| `aleatoric`, columns ending `_ale` | $\\mathbb{E}[\\sigma_n^2]=\\beta_n/(\\alpha_n-1)$, Eq. (25) |\n",
+    "| `epistemic`, columns ending `_epi` | $\\operatorname{Var}(\\mu_n)=\\beta_n/[\\nu_n(\\alpha_n-1)]$, Eq. (26) |\n",
+    "| `total` before a square root | $\\mathbb{E}[\\sigma_n^2]+\\operatorname{Var}(\\mu_n)$, Eq. (19) |\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The four columns of `grid_preds` are $(\\gamma,\\nu,\\alpha,\\beta)$ in the model's target coordinates. In the historical time-plot cells only, the code variable **`gamma` contains observations $y_n$**, while `gamma_pred` contains predictions $\\gamma_n$; these legacy aliases are retained. Quantities after `np.sqrt`, including the local arrays `_ale` and `_epi`, are uncertainty standard deviations. In Gaussian/ensemble sections, `mu_cv` and local `mu` denote Gaussian/ensemble prediction means, not NIG parameters.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "For Eq. (15), write $s_n^2=\\beta_n(1+\\nu_n)/(\\nu_n\\alpha_n)$: SciPy's Student-t uses `df=2*alpha`, `loc=gamma`, and **`scale=s_n`**. The second parameter printed in Eq. (15) is thus a squared scale in SciPy's convention. The historical `pit_figure_gaussian` routine explicitly uses a Gaussian CDF; it does not implement this Student-t CDF. These research cells require the authors' external result files and checkpoints.\n"
+   ]
+  },
