+    "## 3. Original evidential regression model\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Notation key for the paper.** We use the notation of [Schreck et al. (2024)](https://doi.org/10.1175/AIES-D-23-0093.1). For one fixed input $x_n$ and one regression target, the network outputs $(\\gamma_n,\\nu_n,\\alpha_n,\\beta_n)$, with $\\nu_n>0$, $\\alpha_n>1$, and $\\beta_n>0$. The latent mean $\\mu_n$ and latent observation-noise variance $\\sigma_n^2$ follow the NIG distribution in Eqs. (12)–(14); $\\gamma_n$ is the point prediction, not the latent random mean.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "| Quantity in the code | Paper notation | Paper equation |\n",
+    "| --- | --- | --- |\n",
+    "| NIG location, sometimes named `mu`; evaluation field `mean` | $\\mathbb{E}[\\mu_n]=\\gamma_n$ | (24) |\n",
+    "| `aleatoric` | $\\mathbb{E}[\\sigma_n^2]=\\beta_n/(\\alpha_n-1)$ | (25) |\n",
+    "| `epistemic` | $\\operatorname{Var}(\\mu_n)=\\beta_n/[\\nu_n(\\alpha_n-1)]$ | (26) |\n",
