+   "source": [
+    "## Diurnal uncertainty composite following Figure 11\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This additional diagnostic follows the time-of-day presentation in **Figure 11 of [Schreck et al. (2024), *Evidential Deep Learning: Enhancing Predictive Uncertainty Estimation for Earth System Science Applications*](https://doi.org/10.1175/AIES-D-23-0093.1)**. It uses this notebook's existing evidential model and **all held-out test observations**, grouped by their source timestamps into 10-minute clock-time bins across all test dates. The original example predicts friction velocity only, so the composite has one panel. Its short training budget and original split are retained; the figure illustrates this run rather than reproducing the paper's fully trained results.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Within each clock-time bin, the blue and orange curves show the mean observed and predicted friction velocity. Let $B_t$ contain all test observations in clock-time bin $t$. The observed and predicted means are $|B_t|^{-1}\\sum_{n\\in B_t}y_n$ and $|B_t|^{-1}\\sum_{n\\in B_t}\\gamma_n$, with $\\gamma_n=\\mathbb{E}[\\mu_n]$ from **Eq. (24)**. The green and red curves show **conditional RMS standard deviations**, using **Eqs. (25) and (26)**:\n",
+    "\n",
+    "$$\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{|B_t|}\\sum_{n\\in B_t}\\mathbb{E}[\\sigma_n^2]},\\qquad \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{|B_t|}\\sum_{n\\in B_t}\\operatorname{Var}(\\mu_n)}.$$\n",
+    "\n",
+    " Averaging variances before taking their square root keeps all four curves in the same physical units. These uncertainty curves are **not confidence intervals or standard errors for the diurnal means**, and do not include between-observation variation of predicted means, so they are not the variance of the full distribution pooled within a clock-time bin. The CSV includes per-bin counts to make sampling differences visible. Missing bins remain gaps. The source timestamps have no stated timezone; none is assigned.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The figure and its complete summary are saved as high-resolution PNG, SVG, and CSV files for further analysis. The earlier full-test error, coverage, calibration, and chronological diagnostics remain available above."
+   ]
+  },
