+    "| `epistemic` | $\\operatorname{Var}(\\mu_n)$, Eq. (26) |\n",
+    "| `total` | $\\mathbb{E}[\\sigma_n^2]+\\operatorname{Var}(\\mu_n)$, Eq. (19) |\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The uncertainty outputs are **variances**, so their attribution plot labels use these variance expressions rather than standard deviations. In the commented raw-parameter code, `mu, v, alpha, beta` correspond to $(\\gamma_n,\\nu_n,\\alpha_n,\\beta_n)$; the paper's $\\mu_n$ is the latent random mean. The subscript $n$ identifies the per-input output being explained; plots titled Average Attribution average those feature contributions over the chosen observations. Attribution values describe feature contributions to the chosen output, not uncertainty estimates themselves. Matplotlib `alpha` is plotting opacity, unrelated to the NIG shape $\\alpha_n$.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This research notebook requires the authors' external configuration, data, and checkpoint. Its historical Captum workflow has not been rerun here; figures affected by the corrected output labels have been cleared. The current inference-only `predict` API also requires a differentiable adapter before these gradient attribution experiments can run.\n"
